$DIR/test.p:34:16: cannot assign to r["k"]: RO has no method SetIndex
    Library containers such as vec.Vec and hash.Map are indexed through methods.
    x[k] calls x.Index(k), x[k] = v calls x.SetIndex(k, v), and v, ok := x[k]
    calls x.IndexOk(k). The container's type does not have the method this use
    of x[k] needs.
    Add the method to the type, or call another of its methods directly.
    Go builds maps and slices into the language. In Plutonium they are library
    types that own their memory, so the index syntax is lent to them through
    methods.
    To support v, ok := x[k], add:
        func (m *Table) IndexOk(k string) (int, bool) {
            ...
        }
    (see "Indexing library containers" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.11)
    (run "pluto explain E2451" for a longer explanation)
